VALUES (4, 'MCQ: Which network type is best compared to a public library with centralized resource management?', 'A. Client/server network', 'B. Peer-to-peer network', 'C. Personal Area Network', 'D. Wide Area Network', 'A', 'Client/server networks have centralized servers managing resources, similar to a librarian.', 'medium');
VALUES (4, 'Short: Describe one major disadvantage of traditional peer-to-peer networks when scaled to large numbers of users.', 'A. Difficult resource management without central control', 'B. High licensing fees', 'C. Requires cloud infrastructure', 'D. Too much security', 'A', 'Peer-to-peer networks become difficult to manage and secure as they grow large.', 'hard');
VALUES (4, 'MCQ: Which of the following is a characteristic of modern peer-to-peer networks compared to traditional ones?', 'A. Use of the Internet and specialized software', 'B. Operate only on LANs', 'C. No file sharing allowed', 'D. Fully centralized control', 'A', 'Modern P2P networks span the Internet and need special software for file sharing.', 'medium');
VALUES (4, 'Fill in the blank: The original Napster primarily allowed sharing of ______ files over the Internet.', 'A. music', 'B. video', 'C. text documents', 'D. software', 'A', 'Napster was focused on sharing music files globally.', 'easy');
VALUES (4, 'True or False: Client/server networks always require expensive hardware and professional administrators.', 'A. False', 'B. True', 'C. Only in big companies', 'D. Only for cloud networks', 'A', 'While often more complex than peer-to-peer, client/server networks can vary widely in cost and complexity.', 'medium');
VALUES (4, 'MCQ: Which of these is a direct consequence of a network using a server to manage resource sharing?', 'A. Centralized administration and control', 'B. Equal authority of all computers', 'C. No need for resource sharing', 'D. Each computer manages its own resources independently', 'A', 'Servers centralize resource management in client/server networks.', 'medium');
VALUES (4, 'MCQ: Which of the following best describes a Personal Area Network (PAN)?', 'A. A network connecting personal devices within a very small area, typically within a single room', 'B. A large network connecting multiple cities or countries', 'C. A network that connects several Local Area Networks (LANs) within a campus', 'D. A network designed exclusively for servers and data centers', 'A', 'A PAN connects personal devices in a small, localized area, such as a room or around a single person.', 'easy');
VALUES (4, 'MCQ: What is the primary role of a server in a client/server network?', 'A. To manage shared resources and authorize client access', 'B. To operate independently without interacting with other computers', 'C. To share resources directly between clients', 'D. To connect to the internet only', 'A', 'A server manages shared resources and controls access for clients in the network.', 'easy');
VALUES (4, 'True/False: Clients on a client/server network share resources directly with each other without needing a server.', 'A. False', 'B. True', 'C. Only in small networks', 'D. Depends on network size', 'A', 'In client/server networks, resource sharing is mediated by the server, not directly between clients.', 'easy');
VALUES (4, 'Fill in the blank: To function as a server, a computer must run a ________.', 'A. Network Operating System', 'B. Personal Operating System', 'C. Web browser', 'D. Antivirus software', 'A', 'A Network Operating System manages network resources and client access for servers.', 'easy');
VALUES (4, 'MCQ: Which of the following is NOT a function of a Network Operating System (NOS)?', 'A. Control which files users can access', 'B. Manage data for multiple clients', 'C. Restrict user access based on credentials', 'D. Serve as an internet browser', 'D', 'NOS manages network resources and security but does not serve as an internet browser.', 'medium');
VALUES (4, 'Interpretation: 
