VALUES (4, 'MCQ: How do clients and servers typically communicate in a client/server network?', 'A. Via switches and routers', 'B. Direct cable connections only', 'C. Through USB devices', 'D. Using only wireless signals', 'A', 'Switches and routers facilitate communication between clients and servers on a network.', 'medium');
VALUES (4, 'Short answer: Why might it be uncommon for a computer to act as both a client and a server simultaneously?', 'A. It requires significant resources and complex configuration', 'B. It is illegal', 'C. It violates network protocols', 'D. It slows down the internet connection', 'A', 'Acting as both client and server demands more resources and careful configuration, making it less common.', 'hard');
VALUES (4, 'MCQ: Which NOS feature controls when and from where users can access the network?', 'A. Access restrictions and policies', 'B. File sharing protocols', 'C. Network speed optimization', 'D. Hardware diagnostics', 'A', 'NOS can enforce policies that restrict access based on time and location.', 'hard');
