VALUES (4, 'True/False: Peer-to-peer networks are generally more scalable than client/server networks.', 'A. True', 'B. False', 'C. Depends on network size', 'D. Not applicable', 'B', 'Peer-to-peer networks are less scalable because resource management becomes difficult as more computers join, unlike client/server networks.', 'easy');
