VALUES (4, 'What primary problem does device server technology solve for serial devices?', 'A. It replaces serial ports with USB ports', 'B. It provides an easy and economical way to connect serial devices to Ethernet networks', 'C. It eliminates the need for network security', 'D. It converts Ethernet devices into serial devices', 'B', 'Device servers allow serial-only devices to connect to Ethernet networks without complex development.', 'medium');
VALUES (4, 'True or False: Historically, Ethernet interfacing was complex due to multiple proprietary vendor protocols and RFCs.', 'A. True', 'B. False', '', '', 'A', 'Ethernet interfaces involved complex vendor protocols and RFCs, making integration lengthy.', 'medium');
VALUES (4, 'Which of the following reasons explains why some products originally lacked Ethernet interfaces?', 'A. The products did not require network connectivity', 'B. Ethernet was considered too fast', 'C. Development time and expense were not justified', 'D. Ethernet technology was not invented yet', 'C', 'Some vendors thought adding Ethernet was too costly and time-consuming for their product’s use.', 'medium');
VALUES (4, 'Fill in the blank: The evolutionary standpoint states that stable _____ infrastructures have encouraged focus on maximizing productivity beyond IS capacities.', 'A. cloud', 'B. serial', 'C. network', 'D. hardware', 'C', 'As network stability improved, organizations looked to leverage networks for broader productivity gains.', 'medium');
VALUES (4, 'What feature of external device servers is highlighted in their use for device networking?', 'A. They require custom drivers', 'B. They provide serial connectivity for various applications', 'C. They only support wireless connections', 'D. They replace Ethernet entirely', 'B', 'External device servers enable devices with serial ports to connect to Ethernet networks easily.', 'medium');
VALUES (4, 'Why is M2M communication important in the context of device servers?', 'A. Because it allows devices to communicate automatically over networks, improving automation and efficiency', 'B. Because it requires manual user intervention to exchange data', 'C. Because it limits communication to human-operated devices only', 'D. Because it slows down data exchange between devices', 'A', 'M2M enables autonomous data exchange between devices, which enhances operational control and monitoring.', 'medium');
