VALUES (4, 'MCQ: Why is encryption important when connecting devices to a network?', 'A. It speeds up data transmission', 'B. It provides secure communication to protect sensitive data', 'C. It converts serial data to Ethernet', 'D. It limits the number of connected devices', 'B', 'Encryption safeguards data against interception and unauthorized access on networks.', 'medium');
VALUES (4, 'Interpretation: How has the development of network infrastructure influenced device server adoption?', 'A. Stable networks have encouraged integration of legacy devices', 'B. Networks have made device servers obsolete', 'C. Lack of networks delayed device server usage', 'D. Device servers only work on unstable networks', 'A', 'As network reliability improved, organizations sought to connect serial devices via device servers.', 'medium');
