VALUES (4, 'Which of the following is a primary benefit of using Ethernet networks over RS-485 for device communication?', 'A. Shorter cable lengths', 'B. Lower cost of installation', 'C. Greater range and data integrity monitoring', 'D. Higher voltage support', 'C', 'Ethernet networks not only offer a greater communication range than RS-485 but also monitor packet traffic and indicate lost packets, improving data integrity.', 'medium');
VALUES (4, 'True or False: RS-485 allows for multiple devices to be linked using a multidrop network configuration.', 'A. True', 'B. False', 'C. Not specified', 'D. Only on LAN', 'A', 'RS-485 is specifically designed for multidrop communication, enabling multiple serial devices to connect on the same network.', 'medium');
