VALUES (4, 'True or False: Serial technologies guarantee the integrity of data transmission like Ethernet does.', 'A. True', 'B. False', 'C. Only in short distances', 'D. Only with repeaters', 'B', 'Unlike Ethernet, serial communication standards like RS-232 and RS-485 do not include features to guarantee data integrity.', 'medium');
VALUES (4, 'Which example best illustrates an M2M (Machine-to-Machine) application?', 'A. A barcode scanner sending data to a cash register', 'B. A user typing on a keyboard', 'C. A game controller vibrating during gameplay', 'D. A technician manually entering data into a spreadsheet', 'A', 'M2M communication involves direct device-to-device communication, as in the case of a scanner automatically updating a POS system.', 'medium');
